00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.500
{blue}a Watermelon, and {r,ed}a Hospital Visit{大家さんとスイカとお見舞いの日} {calling on someone who is ill; enquiry; inquiry}

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.460
<i>The soft feeling of a futon that has been aired out in the sun.</i>

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:23.400
<i>It’s flat like a rice cracker but ever so fluffy.</i>

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:31.560
<i>As usual, my little sister is busily preparing a delicious dinner.{chiisai (small, little), I guess that makes this a pun?}</i>

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.700
<i>I like this natural routine more than anything else.</i>

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.070
<i>But…</i>

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.030
<i>That’s right.</i>

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:49.780
<i>Today at 7:30 p.m., the dark lord of riches will make his monthly visit.</i>

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.250
Onee-chan, are you okay?!

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.220
Yeah, don’t worry.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.670
I’m fine, I’m fine.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.950
Thank you for the meal.{the synchronousness with which they perform this action is entirely unnerving}

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.410
What should we do?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:22.640
If we pay this month’s rent, next month will be hard on us.{SHOESTRING BUDGET}

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:25.760
But the landlord won’t give us a break, will he?

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:31.870
<i>When we eat dinner, we try to avoid the subject of money.</i>

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.180
<i>This has been our unwritten rule for a long time.</i>

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.040
<i>But today is an exception.</i>

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:49.620
Onee-chan, today I will protect you from the scary demon!

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.680
It’s okay, Asu. Onee-chan will try her best.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:57.700
He’s coming.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:58.860
He’s coming!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.500
Huh?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.230
He didn’t come…

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.520
Does that mean this month’s rent payment is canceled?

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.340
I don’t think it’s that simple…

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.680
He must not be collecting the rent this month.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:32.950
Onee-chan…

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:47.570
That feels good!

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.460
Onee-chan, you’re certainly in a good mood.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:51.310
Yeah!

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:55.140
Without a doubt, the landlord must have decided to not collect the rent anymore.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.790
That’s why I’m feeling so great!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.490
Why do you think that?

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:05.850
He probably won the lottery or something, so he doesn’t need to collect rent anymore.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.260
That’s why he didn’t come by last night.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:12.350
Maybe we won’t have to pay the rent ever again!

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.680
I don’t think things will go that well…

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.800
Hey, look, look.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.030
I’m wearing my swimsuit under my t-shirt.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.370
This way, it doesn’t matter how soaked I get.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.670
You should go change too.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.230
Don’t do that, Onee-chan!

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.300
Wait up!

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.530
Hey, you’re being too loud!

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:37.460
Sorry.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.420
N-No, it’s fine, as long as you understand.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:41.940
Man.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:46.170
I was so relieved when that annoying landlord didn’t come, too.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.310
Ah, that’s right.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:52.030
It was such a relief not having to pay rent this month.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.350
What are you talking about?

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:57.510
The landlord didn’t come by last night saying, “Pay the rent!” right?

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.850
He must have won the lottery—

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.940
Ah, the landlord is in the hospital right now.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.150
He’s hospitalized?

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.370
Yeah.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:11.760
I heard that he fell from somewhere and broke his leg or something.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.220
Is he okay?

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:17.350
I have no idea.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.960
He didn’t even tell anyone,

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.380
and even if someone visited him, he’d just brush them off.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.010
Oh well, I guess it can’t be helped.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.140
He only has himself to blame for his attitude.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.450
No one…

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:37.200
He must be lonely, with no one visiting him.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:39.060
All alone…

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:46.470
So he didn’t win a lottery, and the rent’s not canceled.

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.310
Of course that wouldn’t happen.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.160
I’m pretty stupid, aren’t I?

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.750
That’s what I like about you.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.530
Asu!

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:04.170
But, Onee-chan, you really believed your own explanation, didn’t you?

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.670
Hey, why don’t we go visit the landlord together?

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.380
Yes, let’s go.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.850
Isn’t it a little frightening?

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.280
Yeah, I’m a little bit afraid.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.760
He is a dark lord after all.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:29.110
When he realizes that we’ve only brought one apple…

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.110
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:30.150
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:30.190
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:30.230
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:30.280
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:30.320
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:30.360
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:30.400
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:30.440
Stop screwing around!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:30.480
Stop screwing around!

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:34.800
He’ll probably scold us.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.280
But, we don’t have enough money to buy anything more expensive.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.560
It can’t be helped.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.630
Yes, it’s better than nothing.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:43.480
Probably…

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.740
Yeah! I suppose…

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.400
Mr. Landlord! We’ve come to visit you!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.530
I-Idiots!{tsundere~}{<+Isurugi_Mio> kick the bitch in the teeth <+Isurugi_Mio> j-j-j-jam it in <+Isurugi_Mio> and then he’ll go all deredere}

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.590
Really.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:22.500
This is a hospital, so don’t speak so loudly.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.560
S-Sorry.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.170
Isn’t the landlord using a loud vo—

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:31.290
Ah, um, your leg. Is it okay?

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.230
Does it look okay to you?

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:37.470
They do all these examinations, and smoking’s prohibited.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.010
This is the worst!

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.080
Why don’t you start slicing that apple already?

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.560
Ah, yes!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.270
Here you go.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.490
Just put it on the side for now.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.700
Oh, um…

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.250
It was pretty hot this morning, so I watered the yard.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.420
You weren’t watering the yard, you were playing in the water, right?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.140
Eh? Um, yeah, but…

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:16.790
I wore a swimsuit under my t-shirt, so it’s fine.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.940
That doesn’t change anything!

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.390
S-Sorry.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.970
Well then, we’ll be going now.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:49.120
As we expected, that was pretty scary.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.000
Yes, but…

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.960
I wonder if he ate the apple.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.080
I hope he did.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.820
Hey, Onee-chan.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:06.000
For tonight’s dinner, does burdock salad and seaweed scrambled eggs sound good?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.640
Yeah! I’ll look forward to it.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.600
Solve the follwoing problems.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.850
Asu, go brush your teeth.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:15.460
Okay.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:18.330
What should I do tomorrow?

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.110
What’s wrong?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:40.090
If you put something in between
bread crusts, it's a sandwich.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:40.090
Bread crust

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:40.090
Ham

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:40.090
Bread crust

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:48.590
If we pay the rent for this
month, it's going to be tight.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:48.590
Money

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.200
I’m heading off!

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.560
Ah, wait.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:58.530
Asu, I’m going to visit the landlord again today after school.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:02.010
I might be home late, so don’t worry, okay?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:02.990
Onee-chan…

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.760
I thought about it, and it’s just like you said.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:10.220
Anyone who is hospitalized and has no visitors will feel lonely.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.660
I know I would.

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:15.430
So, I think I’ll go visit him more for the time being.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.800
Yeah, that’s a good idea!

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.060
I’m going now!

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.490
Ah, Asu.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:25.890
You don’t have to force yourself to go!

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:46.890
Asu?!

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:53.750
You see, Yaoichi-obasan asked me to give this watermelon to the landlord.{idk if she’s misreading her line or fucking what, but she sticks a “no” between yaoichi and obasan that might indicate that it's some kind of mutilation of yaoya which means greengrocer and I cbf to figure this shit out so if it's wrong it's fucking wrong and what are you going to do about it.}

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:58.480
If you’re going to visit him every day, then I will too, okay?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.710
Asu!

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.880
S-Stop. That hurts, Onee-chan!

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.920
Hmm, it seems like he’s still in a bad mood.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:15.680
Okay.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.150
Good day!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.900
What the?! You two came again?

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:25.070
Um, Yaoichi-san asked Asu to bring this watermelon as a gift.{八百屋 【やおや】 (n) greengrocer;}

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:29.710
Even though it’s a little small, the skin’s firm, so it must be delicious.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.320
I’ll go cut it right now.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.620
You can eat it whenever you get hungry.

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:43.270
Mr. Landlord, would you like some barley tea?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.260
I brought it from home.

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:49.860
It’s pretty hot today, so why don’t you cool off with this?

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:50.340
Here.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:28.760
Ah, welcome back!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:33.220
Cleaning

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:32.350
Thank you for delivering the watermelon, Asu-chan.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:33.220
No problem.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.340
That old man didn’t eat it, right?

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:41.050
Don’t mind him, he’s always like that.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:42.810
Oh yeah.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:43.940
Here, these are for you.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:47.380
This is my thanks for making that delivery.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.520
It’s meat, so eat a lot and cheer up.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.250
Thanks for the food!

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.210
Amazing! We have quite a feast today!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:06.030
Yes! She really gave us a lot of meat.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.170
Delicious!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.590
<i>I’m truly fortunate.</i>

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.640
<i>No matter how depressed I am,</i>

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:20.810
<i>as long as I get to eat dinner with Asu like this,
those feelings will float away like a cloud.</i>

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.520
<i>And I’ll be able to face tomorrow with a smile.</i>

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:29.750
<i>That way, I’ll definitely have the energy to try my best.</i>

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:32.910
<i>I wonder how the landlord is doing.</i>

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:38.540
<i>Maybe this man who lives alone really doesn’t have anyone to care for him.</i>

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:43.570
<i>Asu probably realized that about him.</i>

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:48.840
Asu, why don’t we visit him every day?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.360
Yeah, let’s do it!

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:30.770
Hello.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.840
Ah, you two visit a lot, don’t you?

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.410
It must be hard to come by every day.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.800
Not at all.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:46.480
Is Mr. Landlord still sleeping?

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:49.100
I’m not sure. He was awake a while ago.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.700
What the, it’s you guys again.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:00.660
Mr. Landlord, I picked some flowers for you today.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.370
Asu picked them from the roadside.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:07.540
Don’t visit me any more!

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.860
I said, stop coming!{definitely tsundere}

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:27.320
I think we troubled him…

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:37.340
Oh no, we have to prepare for the leaking!

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:39.260
Asu! Go get the dishes and pans!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.210
Huh? It’s not leaking.

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.680
Did someone fix it for us?

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:06.440
I heard that he fell from somewhere and broke his leg or something.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.060
For us…

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:17.570
<i>All the time, the landlord’s expression never changed.</i>

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.030
<i>Even when Asu was massaging his back,</i>

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:24.630
<i>or when I tried to get him to say “Ah” while feeding him pudding.</i>

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:27.230
<i>His face always had a lonely look.</i>

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.980
<i>But I have a feeling that he was never annoyed.</i>

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.460
<i>It must be hard to come by every day.</i>

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.460
I get it! That’s why he said that!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:40.260
Don’t visit me any more!

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.100
Onee-chan, that reminds me.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:49.410
I saw him fixing himself up as we came in.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.480
That’s great!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:55.690
I was afraid he would hate me for showing up every day.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:58.640
I didn’t know what I would do if he ended up hating you too.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:00.260
I’m so relieved!

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.440
Onee-chan.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.070
Asu.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:19.450
Good morning!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.040
Mr. Landlord!

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:24.720
Wh-what? Didn’t I tell you guys not to come anymore?{tsun tsun}

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.830
This is our last visit.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:31.270
Please get well soon, and come back to the apartment.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.690
Th-Thank you.{Th is an english phenome}

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:57.630
Today I’m wearing my swimsuit under my t-shirt again.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:03.050
But on a hot day like this, swimming is still
definitely better than just playing with water.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.340
But, Onee-chan…

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.890
This isn’t a pool.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.570
Isn’t this a washbasin?

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:10.600
Don’t mind, don’t mind.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.960
Isn’t it great to have a pool in the yard?

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:17.010
I can also wash your hair while we’re at it.{where the FUCK did the soap come from}

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:20.060
We’ll be scolded by the landlord again.

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:24.920
It’ll be fine because we’re good friends with the landlord now.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.800
Who said we’re good friends?

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.000
Ah, Mr. Landlord.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.830
Congratulations on being released.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:38.960
Look at this mess. What were you guys thinking?

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:41.050
Ah, what should I do?!

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.350
Don’t say, “What should I do?!”

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.760
Ah! Sorry!

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:47.580
Oh yeah, and…

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.510
Pay the rent.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:58.080
In the end, the landlord still collected this month’s rent.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:10.110
But after that, he quietly said, “Thank you for watering the flowers”, right?

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:10.890
Yes.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.800
That’s right, even though on the last day of each month,

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:19.430
the landlord will still transform into the dark lord of riches.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:24.030
Let’s do our best and always stay in this apartment, Asu.

